ovely party which first of all I like  the starting setup and premise which is  river shows up on this ongoing party on  a ship that has been going on for years  that people just kind of drop in and out  of as they will which first of all  immediately reminded me of Hitchhiker's  Guide to the galaxy I think it was the  third book I think it was life the  universe and everything that had the  party that never ended so it reminded me  a little bit of that but then it kind of  matches up to ideas which I mean I  suppose is better than taking an idea  that doesn't work in audio and  stretching it out for a full hour like  the previous one did but the thing is is  that these two ideas don't quite build  on each other properly because it's so  first we have kind of a locked door  mystery kind of thing because we're at  this party it's really hard to get in  and out of and somebody has died and so  we've got a mystery element and then in  addition to that River uncovers that the  people the sorts of people come to this  party the rich the powerful the  influential they fancy themselves the  rulers of the universe and they actually  deliberately and artificially tweak and  manipulate civilizations that have not  that are below a certain technology  level in order to quote-unquote  steer them in the in the right direction  and neither of these are bad ideas but  they don't inherently complement each  other and the story doesn't do a ton to  interweave them now I mentioned birdie  and in the last one in this one  he comes back because it turns out he's  actually one of the member and one of  the members of the rulers of the  universe and it's really weird I mean I  guess they did it to like create some  kind of a through-line between the  previous one and this one I don't think  it helps though because that's the only  thing that connects and honestly he  doesn't add anything and the way he  behaves is so completely different from  the way he behaved last time  explained with